---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import {company,site,publicDeployment as deployment} from '../data/site';
import TeamSection from '../components/TeamSection.astro';
---
<Content title={`About ${company.full} — our company and team`} description={`${company.entity}, operating under ${company.holdingCompany}, develops AI infrastructure in Mead, Oklahoma. Meet the SmartTec leadership and advisory team.`} kicker="Company / People / Purpose" heading="The people behind the infrastructure." lede={`SmartTec is developing data-center services on a ${site.acres}-acre campus in Mead, Oklahoma: shared inference and dedicated GPU servers on SmartTec-owned hardware, alongside colocation for customer-owned equipment.`} meta={[
  {label:'Company',value:company.entity,note:`Operating under ${company.holdingCompany}`},
  {label:'Parent company',value:company.parent,note:'Battery production and energy expertise'},
  {label:'Campus',value:`${site.acres} acres`,note:site.name},
  {label:'Compute proposal',value:deployment.label,note:'Eight Supermicro systems in one building'},
]}>
  <section aria-labelledby="what" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__n">01</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Our focus</span></p>
    <h2 id="what">A practical starting point for AI infrastructure</h2>
    <div class="split"><p>SmartTec is developing its first campus at {site.address}. Buildings A and C provide {site.dataCenterArea.toLocaleString()} sq ft of gross building area for data-center development. Building B supports batteries, utilities and storage. The initial proposal is {deployment.gpus} B300 GPUs in {deployment.systems} Supermicro systems, together in one building. The current budget assumes air-cooled servers with new room/in-row cooling, subject to exact OEM SKU confirmation.</p><p>Each planned service starts with workload, power, cooling, connectivity and tenancy requirements, followed by an agreed installation and service plan. The launch uses grid power, with solar and BESS as a separate later investment. The fleet is proposed; customer availability follows procurement, fit-out and commissioning.</p></div>
    <p>{site.ownership}. {site.ownershipNote}</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="parentage" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__n">02</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Energy and compute</span></p>
    <h2 id="parentage">Connected by a shared campus plan</h2>
    <p>{company.entity} operates under {company.holdingCompany}. {company.parent} is the parent company and battery producer. Its energy expertise connects SmartTec's compute deployment with the longer-term battery, solar and manufacturing plan.</p>
    <div class="cards"><article class="card"><h3>Data-center services</h3><p>SmartTec-owned hosting through shared inference or dedicated single-tenant GPU servers, plus colocation for customer-owned equipment. Allocation and service terms follow validation.</p><a href="/compute">Explore the compute plan →</a></article><article class="card"><h3>Energy infrastructure</h3><p>Grid power first, with shared OG&E service and all-new cooling to validate. Solar and BESS are a later investment with a separate operating and capital case.</p><a href="/power">See power and cooling →</a></article><article class="card"><h3>Campus development</h3><p>Existing buildings anchor the first phase. Planned inverter and battery assembly, solar and storage progress through separate development milestones.</p><a href="/site">Explore Site 01 →</a></article></div>
  </section>
  <TeamSection />
  <section class="is-end" aria-labelledby="talk" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__n">04</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Start a conversation</span></p>
    <h2 id="talk">Bring us the workload you want to run</h2>
    <p>Contact Yasir at <a href="mailto:yasir@smarttec.dev">yasir@smarttec.dev</a> to discuss your deployment, arrange a site visit or connect with the team.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Talk to SmartTec</a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/site">Visit the campus plan</a></div>
  </section>
</Content>
